bodyText:
You must keep the dwelling unit habitable at all times during the tenancy.

It is uninhabitable if it substantially lacks:
- weatherproofing of roof, walls, windows and doors;
- working plumbing;
- approved hot and cold running water connected to approved sewage disposal and safe drinking water as far as you control it;
- adequate heat;
- safe electrical lighting and wiring;
- buildings and grounds safe, clean and free of debris, garbage, rodents and vermin at the start (and areas you control kept that way);
- garbage receptacles and removal (unless a local ordinance or written agreement says otherwise);
- floors, walls, ceilings, stairs and railings in good repair;
- ventilation, air conditioning and appliances you supply in good repair;
- fire safety including a working smoke alarm at the start of each tenancy;
- carbon monoxide alarms where required;
- working locks on entrance doors and window latches;
- a means of unlocking the unit and reaching common areas that includes at least one option other than a tenant portal;
- and, for buildings permitted on or after April 1, 2024, cooling in at least one room.

You may not accept rent free of this duty. You and the tenant may agree in writing that the tenant performs specified repairs or maintenance only on the statute's conditions.
